Verified run_0005 was already stamped final for generic_exp_2 at archived ROC AUC 0.9103940083, superseding run_0001, with candidate hashes matching this branch's starting point.
Implemented the exact task SQL with mandatory equality verification on every snapshot, the anchored +10/+20 pseudo grid, exact future-participant cohorts, 30-day closure gates, qualifying-prefix keyed per-origin feature caches, overlap-adjusted 0.35 weights, and uniform/five-year recency alternatives.
Implemented official-only and pseudo L2 logistic candidates, fixed shallow LightGBM, fixed 50/50 logit blend, and a prequential ridge-Poisson alpha-0.5 expected-count offset, selected only through four embargoed expanding folds, 100 paired timestamp bootstraps, and leave-one-season-out diagnostics.
The measured pre-2005 grid contains 116 nonempty origins and 2,655 rows rather than the proposal's approximate 114/2,438; exact SQL semantics and the specified global grid were retained and the discrepancy was recorded in eval_profile.md and the living documents.
Train-only static replay rejected every augmented candidate: pooled AUC was 0.896710 official-only, 0.895096 pseudo logistic, 0.892844 pseudo recency, 0.875638 LightGBM, 0.895156 blend, and 0.895265 count offset.
The immutable kapso_evaluation tree remained byte-identical. Registered fast rolling evaluation completed all 588 validation and 726 test rows with ROC AUC 0.9111286306, AP 0.7420225398, accuracy 0.8775510204, and F1 0.6727272727.
Iteration 2 technical difficulties: DuckDB emits the SQL CASE label as int32 while the official task table stores int64; explicit int64 normalization was required before exact dtype equality passed. The solution's approximate pseudo sizing contradicted the exact global-grid measurement by 217 rows; retaining the literal grid and documenting the discrepancy resolved the ambiguity. The uncached static debug path took 17.64 seconds rather than the proposed under five minutes and registered rolling ticks grew from 7.64 to 12.14 seconds, but both remained far inside their hard timeouts after the shared origin cache was populated.
